review:
The game itself is incredibly fun with friends and at its core is a very cute, enjoyable, Mafia/Werewolf like game. I wish there was a mixed review button, because the game itself isn't a problem.

The problem comes with the community. This has to be the most idiotic and immature community I've ever seen into a videogame ... ever. And I played a lot of games that are notorious for that, including several MOBAs, TF2, CS:GO, Overwatch etc.

Unlike Mafia/Werewolf, don't attempt to play this game seriously, or your brain will shrink and implode. This is the type of game that you'll get either to play with a group of friends or if you have the humor of a 10yo and memes make you jizz over your keyboard.

95% of the attempts of playing this game seriously with random people result in me smacking my head on the desk and asking myself: "How is this person even sentient ?"

A few examples:

- Every game has 1-2 persons (at least), that are leaving because they're not playing impostors; 
- People that are incapable of typing any coherent sentence;
- People that watch some shitty youtuber/twitch stream  and come in, trying to meme and be funny: "Report red immediately, must be impostor !", kind of guys;
- People that are starting votes at the beginning of rounds for no reason;
- Others will try to kick you off because you outed their impostor friend (Even if they're playing a crewmate!);
- Most people aren't capable of logical reasoning. Short example: Red accuses Pink that he is an impostor in round 2, because he saw Pink kill someone. Pink says the other thing around: "He is lying, I saw Red kill ... he is the Impostor!". Instead of outing both of them in two rounds by two quick votes (thus catching an Impostor with certainty, unless both are trolling ... which is the case sometime), people are just simply skipping that, voting X color because it's ugly to them or because they saw some idiotic meme etc. There is no desire to win the game or create an enjoyable experience for anyone. The game is there just to satisfy juvenile humor. 
- "He is looking funny at me", "He is talking too much and taking the lead in conversations too often" ... "MUST BE IMPOSTOR !!", and other stupid arguments that people use to remove players that are actually trying to play the game from the ship. Nobody asks the most important question in the fucking Universe, when such accusations come up ... "WHY ??????"; 

I could go on and on with examples, but whatever ..

This game seriously makes me worry about the future of humanity.
